Table full name: bigquery-public-data.nhtsa_traffic_fatalities. accident_2015
Column name: state_number Type: INT64 Description: This data element identifies the state in which the crash occurred. The codes are from the General Services Administration’s (GSA) publication of worldwide Geographic Location Codes (GLC). For more info on the codes, please look at <C1/V1/D1/PC1/P1/NM1 State Number> section in the pdf: https://crashstats.nhtsa.dot.gov/Api/Public/ViewPublication/812315
Column name: state_name Type: STRING Description: This data element identifies the state in which the crash occurred. The codes are from the General Services Administration’s (GSA) publication of worldwide Geographic Location Codes (GLC).
Column name: consecutive_number Type: INT64 Description: This data element is the unique case number assigned to each crash. It appears on each data file and is used to merge information from the data files together. xxxxxx Two Characters for State Code followed by Four Characters for Case Number
Column name: number_of_vehicle_forms_submitted_all Type: INT64 Description: number_of_vehicle_forms_submitted_all
Column name: number_of_motor_vehicles_in_transport_mvit Type: INT64 Description: This data element is a count of the number of vehicles in-transport involved in the crash. Legally parked vehicles are not included. 001-999 Number of Vehicle Forms
Column name: number_of_parked_working_vehicles Type: INT64 Description: This data element is a count of the number of parked and working vehicles involved in the crash. 0-999 Number of Parked/Working Vehicles in the Crash
Column name: number_of_forms_submitted_for_persons_not_in_motor_vehicles Type: INT64 Description: This data element is the number of Person Forms (Not a Motor Vehicle Occupant) that are applicable to this case (i.e., non-occupants). 00-99 Number of Persons Not in Motor Vehicles
Column name: number_of_forms_submitted_for_persons_in_motor_vehicles Type: INT64 Description: This data element is a count of the number of Person Level (Motor Vehicle Occupant) Forms that are applicable to this case (i.e., occupants). 000-999 Number of Person Forms
Column name: number_of_persons_in_motor_vehicles_in_transport_mvit Type: INT64 Description: This data element is a count of the number of motorists in the crash. A motorist is a driver, passenger or unknown occupant type of a motor vehicle in-transport. 0-999 Number of Persons in Motor Vehicles In-Transport
Column name: number_of_persons_not_in_motor_vehicles_in_transport_mvit Type: INT64 Description: This data element is a count of the number of non-motorists in the crash. A non-motorist is defined as a pedestrian, a cyclist, an occupant of a motor vehicle not intransport, a person riding a horse, an occupant of an animal drawn conveyance, person associated with non-motorist conveyance (e.g., baby carriage, skate board, wheelchair), or an other non-motorist (e.g., person outside a trafficway, person in a house). 0-98 Number of Persons Not in Motor Vehicles in Transport
Column name: county Type: INT64 Description: This data element records the location of the unstabilized event with regard to the County. The codes are from the General Services Administration’s (GSA) publication of worldwide Geographic Location Codes (GLC). 000 Not Applicable 001-996 Use GSA Geographical Codes 997 Other 998 Not Reported 999 Unknown
Column name: city Type: INT64 Description: This data element records the location of the unstabilized event with regard to the City. The codes are from the General Services Administration’s (GSA) publication of worldwide Geographic Location Codes (GLC). 0000 Not Applicable 0001-9996 GSA Geographical Codes 9997 Other 9898 Not Reported 9999 Unknown
Column name: day_of_crash Type: INT64 Description: This data element records the day of the month on which the crash occurred. 01-31 Day of the Month of the Crash -- Unknown
Column name: day_name Type: STRING Description: This data element records the day of the month on which the crash occurred. 01-31 Day of the Month of the Crash -- Unknown
Column name: month_of_crash Type: INT64 Description: This data element records the month in which the crash occurred. For more info on the codes, please look at <C8A Month of Crash> section in the pdf: https://crashstats.nhtsa.dot.gov/Api/Public/ViewPublication/812315
Column name: month_of_crash_name Type: STRING Description: This data element records the month in which the crash occurred. For more info on the codes, please look at <C8A Month of Crash> section in the pdf: https://crashstats.nhtsa.dot.gov/Api/Public/ViewPublication/812315
Column name: year_of_crash Type: INT64 Description: This data element records the year in which the crash occurred. xxxx Year of the Crash
Column name: day_of_week Type: INT64 Description: This data element records the day of the week on which the crash occurred. 1 Sunday 2 Monday 3 Tuesday 4 Wednesday 5 Thursday 6 Friday 7 Saturday -- Unknown
Column name: day_of_week_name Type: STRING Description: This data element records the day of the week on which the crash occurred. 1 Sunday 2 Monday 3 Tuesday 4 Wednesday 5 Thursday 6 Friday 7 Saturday -- Unknown
Column name: hour_of_crash Type: INT64 Description: This data element records the hour at which the crash occurred. 00-23 Hour -- Not Applicable or Not Notified 99 Unknown
Column name: hour_of_crash_name Type: STRING Description: This data element records the hour at which the crash occurred. 00-23 Hour -- Not Applicable or Not Notified 99 Unknown
Column name: minute_of_crash Type: INT64 Description: This data element records the minutes after the hour at which the crash occurred. 00-59 Minute -- Not Applicable or Not Notified 99 Unknown
Column name: minute_of_crash_name Type: STRING Description: This data element records the minutes after the hour at which the crash occurred. 00-59 Minute -- Not Applicable or Not Notified 99 Unknown
Column name: national_highway_system Type: INT64 Description: This data element identifies whether this crash occurred on a trafficway that is part of the National Highway System. 0 This Section is Not on the National Highway System 1 This Section is on the National Highway System 9 Unknown
Column name: national_highway_system_name Type: STRING Description: This data element identifies whether this crash occurred on a trafficway that is part of the National Highway System. 0 This Section is Not on the National Highway System 1 This Section is on the National Highway System 9 Unknown
